Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. FARMHOUSE - MONDAY - BEFORE DAWN

The forgotten timer rings at four. Elias silences it. His hand shakes as he fills the kettle. Zoe takes the kettle without touching him.

ZOE
You said tomorrow. His name first.

ELIAS
Sam. Samuel Mercer. Twenty-two when he died.

She sits. He tells it in pieces.

BRIEF MEMORY IMAGES, confined to his account: a saloon with one mismatched door; Sam spotting a man crossing twice with an unlit cigarette; eighteen months of remembered registrations and bad jokes.

ELIAS
He broke the instruction and warned me.

ZOE
Compromised the car and saved you. Both were true.

The images fragment: failing corridor light, chained exit, too many armed men for a brief naming two crews. Sam moves into the attack. Elias reaches him.

ELIAS
He told me where the car was. I said I was taking him with me.

ZOE
Did he believe you?

ELIAS
No. I'd taught him not to lie about the route.

The memory stops. Rain against the farmhouse window.

ZOE
Then what?

ELIAS
I finished the operation.

ZOE
Jackie's story said you destroyed both crews.

ELIAS
She didn't exaggerate. I used the work we'd done. Mac benefited. I didn't know the connection then. I still can't prove who meant what.

ZOE
You killed people who didn't kill Sam.

ELIAS
Yes.

ZOE
That isn't justice.

ELIAS
No.

He takes her half-full mug and empties it.

ZOE
You didn't ask. I was still drinking it.

He turns the mug upright and refills the kettle.

ELIAS
I stayed driving because I could follow instructions and call it harmless.

Zoe writes: SAMUEL MERCER. SAM. TWENTY-TWO.

ZOE
Loyalty isn't the same as fault. Stop talking like caring about you killed him.

ELIAS
He should have let it hit me.

ZOE
That's grief.

He starts to rise; shoulder pain stops him. He looks at the back door, then chooses to sit again.

ELIAS
Blame gave me a rule. Don't train anyone. Don't let anyone stand beside me.

ZOE
Punishment. I'm not Sam. You don't get to decide how far I'm allowed to learn because you see him.

Later, after sleep, Elias finds her watching the road. Her notebook remains closed.

ELIAS
I won't train you because you remind me of him. I won't refuse because you do, either.

She considers it.

ZOE
Almost sensible.

He lays the notes copied from Reyes's phone on the table without activating it. Together they mark probable roles, not certain biographies. She adds: SAM — BEFORE. NOT THE SAME.
